From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:46:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Keep the fetch timing of a document whose body ends
 with a network error

The parser recorded the fetch timing of a document only when its body
ended without a network error. That condition dates from when the timing
came with a successful end only; it now comes with every end. A document
whose body ends with a network error is still parsed and shown as far as
it got, but its navigation timing entry kept the zeros it was queued with
when the response arrived. Error pages return before this point, so record
the timing whenever the document gets this far.

Net reports a body cut short by the connection as complete today; it will
report it as a network error.

Validation: New test `tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/navigation-timing-network-error.html` passes with `net: End a body cut short by the connection with a network error`; with it but without this patch, `fetchStart` is 0.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent wrote this patch and its test following docs/fetch-p4a-truncated-body-audit-2026-10-22.md in the workspace, and applied an independent review's findings)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/script/dom/servoparser/mod.rs      |  4 +---
 tests/wpt/mozilla/meta/MANIFEST.json          | 11 ++++++++++
 .../navigation-timing-network-error.html      | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../resources/document-network-error.py       | 17 +++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 50 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/navigation-timing-network-error.html
 create mode 100644 tests/wpt/mozilla/tests/mozilla/resources/document-network-error.py

diff --git a/components/script/dom/servoparser/mod.rs b/components/script/dom/servoparser/mod.rs
index df1d2ba7e33..84fcb8c5bdc 100644
--- a/components/script/dom/servoparser/mod.rs
+++ b/components/script/dom/servoparser/mod.rs
@@ -1658,9 +1658,7 @@ impl ParserContext {
         let mut realm = enter_auto_realm(cx, &*document);
         let cx = &mut realm;
 
-        if status.is_ok() {
-            document.set_resource_fetch_timing(timing);
-        }
+        document.set_resource_fetch_timing(timing);
 
         if let Some(parser) = parser {
             parser.last_chunk_received.set(true);
